{"bookId":"el-b13","questions":[{"id":"el-b13-elq-1a92612b8b76bbd0","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t739-0","type":"mcq","text":"Tell which is the example of simple harmonic motion","options":["up and down motion of a leaf in water pond","motion of a ceiling fan","motion of hands of clock","movement of honey bee"],"correctIndex":0,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-ac9185a24280b303","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t739-0","type":"mcq","text":"What mathematical expression relates frequency to period?","options":["f=T","f=2T","f=1/T","1/f=1/T"],"correctIndex":2,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-6fd8652f8268597e","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t739-0","type":"mcq","text":"If a wave frequency increases, its period __________.","options":["decreases","increases","fluctuates","remains the same"],"correctIndex":0,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-66ae1785c4256f4a","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t739-0","type":"mcq","text":"The __________ of a wave can be used to determine how much energy is being transferred by the wave.","options":["speed","period","amplitude","frequency"],"correctIndex":2,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-b1af8f4688bd67a6","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t739-0","type":"mcq","text":"In simple harmonic motion, the restoring force must be proportional to the","options":["amplitude","frequency","velocity","displacement"],"correctIndex":3,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-5e15fe4107b1809a","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topicId":"el-b13-t1100-1","type":"mcq","text":"Time period of a loaded spring is directly proportional to the","options":["square root of mass (m)","both mass and force constant","square root of force constant (k)","none of the above"],"correctIndex":0,"page":3,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b13-elq-1348ae987346b5ef","chapterId":"el-b13-c10","topi